# GH#4 8B3 (task#73): the two repo IPlugAPP forks keep the pinned upstream body BYTE-IDENTICAL
# (verified by tools/check_host_override_drift.py, which pins the SHA-256 of the entire
# upstream->override unified diff). The upstream iPlug 2 TUs carry trailing whitespace in their
# banner / comment lines, which is inherited into the fork unchanged. Normalizing that whitespace
# would break the byte-identical body and inflate the curated diff, so we instead apply a NARROW
# -whitespace exception to exactly these two derivative files: git diff --check ignores whitespace
# errors in them, so the repo's whitespace hygiene gate stays strict for every OTHER source file
# while correctly distinguishing "inherited upstream whitespace" from a real authoring defect.
host/iPlug_app_override.cpp      -whitespace
host/iPlug_app_host_override.cpp -whitespace
